        <UserObject label="D1" tooltip="D1 - Two platforms, not one&#xa;Decision: keep the trusted nightly warehouse; add a lakehouse for event and integration use cases.&#xa;Alternatives: migrate everything to the lakehouse; add near-real-time loads to the warehouse.&#xa;Why: no big-bang migration risk; each platform does what it is best at.&#xa;Revisit when: most consumers need sub-day freshness.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0001-two-platforms-not-one.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-347">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="34" width="34" x="1183" y="240" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D2" tooltip="D2 - Temporal ODS family&#xa;Decision: separate current, effective-dated, future-dated, history and full ODS sharing one code base.&#xa;Alternatives: a single SCD2 staging table; snapshots only.&#xa;Why: back-dated corrections and future-dated changes are handled without corrupting current state; full replay is possible.&#xa;Trade-off: more databases to run, mitigated by one commit promoted to all.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0002-temporal-ods-family.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-348">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="1146" y="1113" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D3" tooltip="D3 - Dependency-tiered batch&#xa;Decision: jobs start when their predecessors finish (dependency graph with gates); a small number of anchor jobs start on a clock.&#xa;Alternatives: fixed clock schedule; one sequential chain.&#xa;Why: independent work runs in parallel, the critical path shrinks, completion adapts to daily volume.&#xa;Trade-off: the dependency graph must be maintained as configuration.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0003-dependency-tiered-batch.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-349">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="1146" y="663" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D4" tooltip="D4 - Federation over replication&#xa;Decision: the lakehouse reads conformed dimensions from the warehouse at query time through a few governed views.&#xa;Alternatives: replicate dimensions into Delta; CDC copy.&#xa;Why: one version of the truth, no sync lag, no duplicate pipelines.&#xa;Guardrails: approved views only, resolve keys at ETL time, monitor latency and source load.&#xa;Revisit when: concurrency or latency targets are missed, then materialize.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0004-federation-over-replication.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-350">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="34" width="34" x="1183" y="2385" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D5" tooltip="D5 - Blocking vs alerting data quality&#xa;Decision: a blocking gate before the warehouse publish; alert-only checks in the lakehouse.&#xa;Why: enterprise reporting should show yesterday&#39;s good data rather than today&#39;s bad data; operational integrations must keep flowing and reconcile later.&#xa;Alternatives: block everywhere; alert everywhere.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0005-blocking-vs-alerting-dq.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-351">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="705" y="2218" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D6" tooltip="D6 - BI tool by audience&#xa;Decision: composite BI model for the broad governed audience; live SQL dashboard for a small ops team; imported dashboards for lakehouse business users.&#xa;Why: match freshness, row-level security and cost to who is reading.&#xa;Alternatives: one tool and one refresh mode for everyone.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0006-bi-tool-by-audience.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-352">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="2326" y="2693" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D7" tooltip="D7 - Medallion only where it adds value&#xa;Decision: an integration gets Bronze/Silver/Gold only if it builds history, has an analytical audience and answers questions no other source can. One integration is deliberately skipped.&#xa;Why: avoids building and running models nobody uses.&#xa;Revisit when: a new audience or question appears.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0007-selective-medallion.md" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-353">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="2326" y="2183" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
		<UserObject label="D8" tooltip="D8 - Change detection by content compare&#xa;Decision: detect changes by comparing content (set-based compare, or row hash for wide entities), excluding volatile columns such as load stamps.&#xa;Alternatives: source timestamps; full nightly reload; database-native CDC.&#xa;Why: timestamps produce false changes and miss real ones; downstream feeds should receive only true changes.&#xa;Trade-off: compare cost grows with width and volume; excluded-column list must be maintained.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0008-change-detection-strategy.md" id="dec8">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="650" y="1560" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D9" tooltip="D9 - Idempotent loads and safe re-runs&#xa;Decision: every load is safe to run twice. Watermarks advance only after full success; upserts instead of blind inserts; additive merges only with a run log that rejects already-processed inputs.&#xa;Alternatives: manual cleanup before re-runs; truncate-and-reload everything.&#xa;Why: any failed job can be re-run without analysis, with no gaps and no double counting.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0009-idempotent-loads.md" id="dec9">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="1140" y="772" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D10" tooltip="D10 - Kimball dimensional model&#xa;Decision: star schema / constellation with conformed dimensions, SCD Type 2 where history matters, role-playing dimensions and several fact types.&#xa;Alternatives: 3NF enterprise model; Data Vault; reporting on raw views.&#xa;Why: intuitive for a large self-service audience and BI tools; consistent KPIs; fast queries.&#xa;Trade-off: ETL build effort; schema changes ripple through the model.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0010-kimball-dimensional-model.md" id="dec10">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="280" y="2220" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D11" tooltip="D11 - Defense-in-depth security&#xa;Decision: layered controls: schema separation by sensitivity tier, row-level security in BI, DirectQuery for highly restricted facts, restricted data kept out of federation, data minimization for feeds.&#xa;Alternatives: row-level security only; separate physical databases per tier.&#xa;Why: a failure in one layer does not expose data.&#xa;Trade-off: role mappings must stay in sync across layers.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0011-defense-in-depth-security.md" id="dec11">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="1140" y="1636" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D12" tooltip="D12 - Bronze captures transient source data&#xa;Decision: capture every inbound payload as received, append-only, before it is transformed, encrypted or forwarded.&#xa;Why: some sources keep no history; without capture, trend analysis and replay are impossible.&#xa;Trade-off: retention cost; raw sensitive data in Bronze must be governed.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0012-bronze-captures-transient-sources.md" id="dec12">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="2310" y="1410" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="D13" tooltip="D13 - Fact and dimension design patterns&#xa;Decision: consolidated facts with a source-type column when several systems record the same event; junk dimensions for low-cardinality flags; weighted bridges for many-to-many; role-playing dimensions.&#xa;Alternatives: one fact per source; flags on facts; unweighted bridges.&#xa;Why: one place to query, correct totals, leaner facts.&#xa;Click to open the ADR." link="https://github.com/srimarrivada/Hybrid-HR-Data-Platform-Reference-Architecture/blob/main/docs/adr/0013-fact-design-patterns.md" id="dec13">
          <mxCell parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#FBBF24;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FBBF24;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;shadow=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="28" width="28" x="411" y="2220" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-354" parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-346" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=34;fillColor=#B71C1C;fontColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#7F1D1D;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;align=left;spacingLeft=14;swimlaneFillColor=#FFFAFA;rounded=1;arcSize=1;collapsible=1;" value="FAILURE &amp;amp; RECOVERY PATHS: What happens when things go wrong (Click a card to jump to that section)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="2320" x="40" y="4200" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="34" width="900" x="40" y="4200" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-360" parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-354" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#7F1D1D;" value="&lt;b&gt;D1–D13&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;(gold circles) = Design decisions: Hover for the trade-off, click for the ADR.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;F1–F5&lt;/b&gt; = Failure paths: Click to jump to the affected section" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="2300" x="10" y="148" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" connectable="0" parent="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-354" style="group" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="2300" x="10" y="44" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;F1 - Nightly run fails part-way&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;• Extraction window is NOT advanced (postload runs only on full success)&lt;br&gt;• Next run re-extracts the same window → no data gaps&lt;br&gt;• Resume from the failed step using restart flags" link="data:action/json,{&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;scroll&quot;:{&quot;cells&quot;:[&quot;bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-69&quot;]}}]}" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-355">
          <mxCell parent="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF5F5;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="86" width="452" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;F2 - DQ gate below threshold&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;• Publish stopped · previous warehouse version stays live&lt;br&gt;• BI keeps yesterday&#39;s import · alert raises a ticket&lt;br&gt;• Fix the data, then re-run only the publish step" link="data:action/json,{&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;scroll&quot;:{&quot;cells&quot;:[&quot;bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-201&quot;]}}]}" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-356">
          <mxCell parent="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF5F5;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="86" width="452" x="462" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;F3 - Integration record or API call fails&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;• Record marked FAILED, the batch continues&lt;br&gt;• Token refresh + retries · scheduled retry or manual reprocess&lt;br&gt;• Replay from Bronze / raw event archive" link="data:action/json,{&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;scroll&quot;:{&quot;cells&quot;:[&quot;bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-152&quot;]}}]}" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-357">
          <mxCell parent="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF5F5;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="86" width="452" x="924" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;F4 - Federation slow or enterpriswarehouse unavailable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;• Lakehouse keeps its last good Gold layer&lt;br&gt;• Unresolved worker → unknown-member key, reconciled after DW publish; alert if still unresolved&lt;br&gt;• If it keeps happening: materialize the hot views (D4)" link="data:action/json,{&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;scroll&quot;:{&quot;cells&quot;:[&quot;bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-250&quot;]}}]}" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-358">
          <mxCell parent="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF5F5;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="86" width="452" x="1386" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;F5 - Late or back-dated source changes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr&gt;• Effective-dated ODS catches back-dated corrections → merged into current&lt;br&gt;• SCD2 history corrected, not overwritten&lt;br&gt;• Future-dated changes held until their effective date (D2)" link="data:action/json,{&quot;actions&quot;:[{&quot;scroll&quot;:{&quot;cells&quot;:[&quot;bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-116&quot;]}}]}" id="bVKumJbvJyEJEweoQE7_-359">
          <mxCell parent="EH1S9GchiQGYpskucD9f-0" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF5F5;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="86" width="452" x="1848" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
